{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-hygiene-access"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Affordable hygiene/disinfectant active-ingredient commercialization for water-scarce and poor-sanitation-infrastructure markets"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :hygiene-disinfectant/commercialization
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:public-health :water-safety :affordability :consumer-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :hygiene-access-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "HygieneAccessAdvisor ⊣ Hygiene Access Operations Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A COORDINATION/PROPOSAL-LAYER
 business actor -- NOT a real chemical-manufacturing control system,
 NOT a real regulatory or medical authority, and NOT literal
 real-world sales infrastructure -- that commercializes two low-cost
 hygiene/disinfectant active ingredients (sodium hypochlorite NaOCl
 and isopropylmethylphenol IPMP) as affordable products for
 water-scarce / poor-sanitation-infrastructure markets (India,
 Gulf/Arabia/MENA, South & Southeast Asia), covering the full chain:
 formulation-batch logging, packaging design, market-entry/pricing
 (go-to-market), marketing-claim substantiation, and
 distribution-channel coordination. Seven ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment` /
 `:propose-packaging-design` / `:propose-market-entry` /
 `:propose-marketing-claim`), all `:effect :propose` only. Nineteen
 concrete HARD governor checks (plus one SOFT confidence/high-stakes
 gate) elaborate this blueprint's own invariants: propose-only effect,
 closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct
 formulation/filling-line-equipment control), permanent
 line-actuate block, permanent certification-decision block (this
 actor never itself grants a chemical-safety/medical/regulatory
 certification -- e.g. India CDSCO/BIS, GCC conformity bodies, ASEAN
 member-state regulators), permanent no-toxic-co-formulation block
 (sodium hypochlorite + an acid-bearing or ammonia-bearing
 co-ingredient is a structurally unrepresentable toxic chlorine-gas/
 chloramine-gas hazard, mirroring etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yakushi's
 own G22), independent formulation/filling-line-equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-weight recompute against the batch's own logged
 weight, double-schedule guard, product-type validation, active-
 ingredient-authorized-for-product-type validation, active-ingredient
 concentration efficacy-window validation (G21 analog, per-product-
 type closed window: sodium-hypochlorite 0.5-1.5% for
 water-purification-drops / 0.05-0.5% for surface-disinfectant,
 isopropylmethylphenol 0.1-0.3% for antibacterial-soap), off-spec-rate
 plausibility validation, BOP-appropriate packaging-format validation,
 independent market-entry-country-approval validation (ground truth,
 not self-report -- any real deployment would still need the
 applicable local regulatory approval this actor does not itself
 grant), independent per-product-type affordability-price-ceiling
 validation, independent distribution-channel-partner-licensing
 validation, and independent marketing-claim-substantiation validation
 against a closed WHO/CDC-style claim set (a first-class ethical
 guardrail against unsubstantiated health claims to a vulnerable
 population). Safety-concern flagging ALWAYS escalates to a human
 go-to-market coordinator, as do market-entry and marketing-claim
 proposals (always high-stakes, never in any phase's auto set);
 `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
